# SYNCED FROM AI-Handbook — do not edit in a consumer repo. Local edits are overwritten by the next sync and their reasoning is lost; change the handbook instead.
# Per-plan review-loop evidence: the round snapshots `plan-review.mjs` writes
# under .agents/reviews/<slug>/.
#
# EPHEMERAL BY CONTRACT. A fresh container legitimately has none of it, and
# re-running the round is the documented remedy rather than a workaround. What
# must survive a loop is the approved plan itself, committed on the
# implementation branch, and the approval comment on the workstream issue.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `plan-review.mjs` writes an ignore file for the
# directories a plan loop creates, but only once it has run; a checkout that
# has not yet run one was covered by nothing, and an ordinary `git add -A`
# staged a snapshot of the material under review. (AI-Handbook #91 round 1,
# where the uncovered directory was the code loop's; the code loop is gone and
# the same hole remains for the plan loop.)
#
# WHY THERE ARE TWO COPIES. Git does not follow a symlinked .gitignore, so a
# pointer is impossible and a real file at each root is the only option. The
# handbook mirrors this one at .agents/reviews/.gitignore, and
# scripts/check-root-wiring.mjs compares the pattern lines so the duplication
# is enforced rather than merely intended. Edit THIS copy; the root follows.
*
!.gitignore
